# Upstream anatomy source — fetched, never vendored.
#
# Startup.blend alone is ~293 MB, past GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, and
# the push would be rejected outright. Both are downloads anyone can repeat from
# the Z-Anatomy project, and the README's asset-pipeline section says exactly
# where to put them. What this repository ships is the *output*: the .glb files
# in public/anatomy/ and the reports the manifest is built from.
tools/asset-pipeline/vendor/Z-Anatomy/
tools/asset-pipeline/vendor/Z-Anatomy.zip

# Coworker instructions for AI agents — kept local, not published.
AGENTS.md

# CI build artefacts downloaded for local testing.
#
# `gh run download <id> -n linux-packages -D ci-linux` drops the release
# bundles here — an AppImage and a .deb, ~235 MB together. They are the
# output of a run that already exists on GitHub, reproducible with one
# command, and have no business in the history.
ci-linux/

# Piper voice models, downloaded on first use by the local voice experiment
# (branch `experiment/voice`). ~60 MB each and fetched on demand — the same reason
# the anatomy source above is not vendored.
engine/voices/

# Core dumps.
#
# WebKitGTK's renderer can dump core on teardown, and the file lands wherever
# the process was started from — `src-tauri/` for `tauri dev`. One of these was
# **7 GB**: it is a snapshot of the whole address space, which for a webview
# means every texture and every page it had loaded. Ignored rather than merely
# deleted because the size is the danger; a single careless `git add -A` would
# put it somewhere `git rm` cannot take it back from.
core
core.*
